> Is there a way in which I can disable a individual user's mail, that is any 
> mail addressed to a particular user is returned to the sender.  I only 
> want to do this to a couple of users on the system who never check their 
> mail and are subscribed to a million list serves and hogging up my /usr.
> 
> Thanks 
> 
Thanks for everyone for their prompt responses.  Three main solutions 
were suggested.

1. Change the ownership on the /usr/spool/mail/USER file to root.

2. Setting a quota on /usr for the USER

3. Modifying the aliase file and adding an entry for the user as
   user:/dev/null

Thanks again.

