Thanks to Randy Hayman (haymanR@icefog.alaska.edu) and Enrique Sanchez Vivar
<evivar@eniac.rhon.itam.mx> for their responses.

Both say that turning on enhanced security will cause passwords to expire.
This is true, unless you modify /etc/auth/system/default and change u_life
and u_exp to 0.  Then it won't automatically expire passwords.

This is good.

