Date: Mon, 17 Jul 1995 23:06:58 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: No auto restart
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96075321606560

 
The problem:

> My Alpha 3000/300 recently upgraded to v3.2a, firmware v6.0, no
> longer automatically restarts after powering down.  It happily boots
> when requested to at the console command prompts, so I have to 
> assume it's a prob with the environment variables.

<Listing of environment variables deleted>

In the end, the environment variables were not to blame.  It seems
on this *particular* model, there is a jumper inside the system which
needed to be switched.  The system now restarts beautifully.

It also seems to be unique to this system that the AUTO_ACTION 
variable can be set to HALT, BOOT or RESTART.  The RESTART option
is supposed to boot the system when it has not shutdown cleanly, as
with a power failure, whereas BOOT will not.

Also, I was in error about the BOOT_OSFLAGS variable being pertinent
to VMS systems only.  For OSF, it determines the run level the system
will be booted to.

Many thanks to those who responded.

Cheers,
Lyn

